/// os_scheduler_sim — a preemptive round-robin scheduler over demand-paged
/// memory.
///
/// Four processes arrive on a staggered schedule and run burst programs of
/// compute phases and page references. The scheduler (`os/sched`) gives the
/// head of its ready queue one quantum at a time; a reference to a page that is
/// not resident traps into the pager (`os/memory`), which takes a frame by the
/// CLOCK second-chance policy and blocks the process while the page is fetched.
/// The two subsystems meet there: paging decides who the scheduler can run, and
/// the schedule decides which pages get a second chance.
///
/// The program prints the machine and the fixture, a trace of the opening
/// ticks, what each process cost, the system totals, and the frame table the
/// policy left behind.
module testapi/main;

import os/report as report;

pub fn main() -> . { report.run() }
